<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<exercise xml:id="problem-topologies-induced-by-p-metrics" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>
    Topologies induced by <m> p </m>-metrics
  </title>
  
  <statement>
    <p>
      Show that for all <m> 1 \leq p \leq \infty </m>, the <m> p </m>-metrics <m> d_{ p } \colon \R^{ n } \times \R^{ n } \to \R </m> induce the same metric topology on <m> n </m>-dimensional real coordinate space <m> \R^{ n } </m>.
    </p>
  </statement>
  
  <hint>
    <p>
      You may find (b) of <xref ref="problem-norm-equivalence"/> useful.
    </p>
  </hint>
  
  <!-- <solution>
    <p>
      We will show that any <m> p </m>-metric induces the Euclidean topology <m> \tau_{ d } </m> on <m> \R^{ n } </m>. Indeed, fix <m> 1 \leq p \leq \infty </m>, and note that (b) of <xref ref="problem-norm-equivalence"/> implies that there are positive real numbers <m> A , B \in \opint{ 0 }{ \infty } </m> so that
      
      <md>
        A \norm{ \vect{ v } }_{ p } \leq \norm{ \vect{ v } } \leq B \norm{ \vect{ v } }_{ p }
      </md>
      
      for all vectors <m> \vect{ v } \in \R^{ n } </m>. let <m> U \subseteq \R^{ n } </m>, and suppose first that <m> U \in \tau_{ d_{ p } } </m> be open in the metric topology <m> \tau_{ d_{ p } } </m> induced by the <m> p </m>-metric <m> d_{ p } </m>. Then for each point <m> \vect{ u } \in U </m>, there is a positive real number <m> r \gt 0 </m> so that
      
      <md>
        \setmid{ \vect{ x } \in \R^{ n } }{ \norm{ \vect{ x } - \vect{ u } }_{ p } \lt r } \subseteq U
      </md>.
      
      We observe that
      
      <md>
        \setmid{ \vect{ x } \in \R^{ n } }{ \norm{ \vect{ x } - \vect{ u } } \lt A r } \subseteq \setmid{ \vect{ x } \in \R^{ n } }{ \norm{ \vect{ x } - \vect{ u } }_{ p } \lt r } \subseteq U
      </md>.
      
      Thus <m> U \in \tau_{ d } </m> is open in the Euclidean topology <m> \tau_{ d } </m>.
    </p>
    
    <p>
      Conversely, now suppose that <m> U \in \tau_{ d } </m> is open in the Euclidean metric. Then for each point <m> \vect{ u } \in U </m>, there is a positive real number <m> r \gt 0 </m> so that
      
      <md>
        \setmid{ \vect{ x } \in \R^{ n } }{ \norm{ \vect{ x } - \vect{ u } } \lt r } \subseteq U
      </md>.
      
      We observe that
      
      <md>
        \setmid{ \vect{ x } \in \R^{ n } }{ \norm{ \vect{ x } - \vect{ u } }_{ p } \lt \frac{ r }{ B } } \subseteq \setmid{ \vect{ x } \in \R^{ n } }{ \norm{ \vect{ x } - \vect{ u } } \lt r } \subseteq U
      </md>.
      
      Thus <m> U \in \tau_{ d_{ p } } </m> is open in the metric topology <m> \tau_{ d_{ p } } </m> induced by the <m> p </m>-metric <m> d_{ p } </m>. 
    </p>
    
    <p>
      In summary, we have shown that <m> U \in \tau_{ d_{ p } } </m> if and only if <m> U \in \tau_{ d } </m>, so that <m> \tau_{ d_{ p } } = \tau_{ d } </m>.
    </p>
  </solution> -->
</exercise>
